WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.520
Hey Youtubers it’s Charlie and this week,
Game Of Thrones totally went there.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:08.380
We got to see a Bran for the first time this
season and a couple new characters from the

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:12.420
books and two really big plot events went
down.

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:15.000
And a quick reminder that round 2 of the giveaway
starts now.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.590
All you have to do is be a subscriber and
leave a comment.

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:25.779
Because there’s so many WTF moments, let’s
just get right into the top 5.

00:00:25.779 --> 00:00:28.310
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
the episode yet.

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:32.940
But Number 5 - Ramsay Snow takes Theon and
heads for Moat Cailin.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:36.930
This is a little different that the books,
but essentially Ramsay is trying to get recognized

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:39.160
as an official heir of the dreadfort.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:41.860
In order to do that, he has to take Moat Cailin
in the north.

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:46.700
It’s going to bring them closer to Theon’s
sister and her force of Iron Born, so it seems

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:50.700
like they’re setting up a big battle between
the flayed men and the ironborn later this

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:51.700
season.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:54.670
Think of it as a slightly less epic version
of the battle that’s shaping up between

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:56.010
the wildlings and the Night’s Watch.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:01:00.090
I thought it was interesting that Theon just
found out about the Red Wedding for the first

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:01.090
time.

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:04.180
And I have to give a bonus shoutout to the
hunting scene at the beginning.

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:09.150
Those two women, the one shooting the bow
and the one being shot, were the girls Ramsay

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:12.050
used to torture Theon with sex last season.

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:14.479
Number 4 - The Jousting Dwarves At The Purple
Wedding

00:01:14.479 --> 00:01:17.960
Everyone had been asking me if the show was
going to use them since they were such a defining

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:20.320
moment of the wedding banquet.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:24.010
But I had no idea and was just as surprised
as everyone else when they came pouring out

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:25.400
of the lion’s mouth.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:32.780
As messed up as it was to degrade the dwarves,
did you see the looks of horror and rage on

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:34.470
everyone’s faces.

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:35.780
Even Tywin was pissed off.

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:39.659
But it was Lady Olenna’s face that was the
best.

00:01:39.659 --> 00:01:41.990
Just pure daggers shooting from her eyes.

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:45.540
I didn’t see anyone that resembled Penny,
one of the dwarves from the ceremony that

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:46.649
has some dialogue in the book.

00:01:46.649 --> 00:01:49.600
Let me know if you spotted her.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:53.420
The music that played under all this was the
rains of castamere if you didn’t hear it

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:54.420
right away.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:02:00.450
There were a few versions of it throughout
the wedding, but it was playing in the chapel

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:05.759
during the ceremony, when the singers came
out, during the jousting and during Joffrey’s

00:02:05.759 --> 00:02:06.759
death scene.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:11.599
I’ll say the flat out most disturbing moment
was when the dwarf was skull fuck*ng the wolf’s

00:02:11.599 --> 00:02:12.599
head.

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:18.650
That was just awful.

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:22.810
Number 3 - Bran Wargs With The Tree And Sees
Everything

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:27.290
It was hard to tell but Bran was actually
seeing everything the weirwoods had seen all

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:28.290
over the planet.

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:31.280
That’s why he could see the north and King’s
landing.

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:36.040
He also saw a side shot of the greenseer,
who gave him instructions where to find him.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:39.015
Everyone keeps asking me about coldhands,
and we might find out if he’s going to appear

00:02:39.015 --> 00:02:40.015
next week.

00:02:40.015 --> 00:02:43.730
I was also super excited to finally get an
answer about the dragon flying over king’s

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:44.730
landing.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.110
Bran saw it as it happened in the past.

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:50.989
So I’m going to be optimistic and say he
was seeing on of the great Targaryen dragons,

00:02:50.989 --> 00:02:54.600
maybe it could have been Balerion the black
dread.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:56.220
He was the biggest in recorded history.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:57.220
I’ll try to explain more about the Bloodraven
and greenseeing in my bonus video next week.

00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:00.319
Number 2 - Joffrey Degrades Everyone at the
Banquet

00:03:00.319 --> 00:03:02.849
It takes real talent to be that awful.

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:07.129
I was surprised he didn’t pick on Sansa
more, but if Tyrion hadn’t been there he

00:03:07.129 --> 00:03:08.239
probably would have.

00:03:08.239 --> 00:03:13.519
If it wasn’t clear, they were just trying
to show that Tyrion had the most reason to

00:03:13.519 --> 00:03:15.370
want him dead.

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:20.379
Everyone at the feast saw him defy Joffrey.

00:03:20.379 --> 00:03:23.060
Regardless of how Joffrey died.

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:25.950
Tyrion is taking the blame for now.

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:31.709
One of my favorite Joffrey lines from the
feast was “There has been too much amusement

00:03:31.709 --> 00:03:32.709
here today”.

00:03:32.709 --> 00:03:34.120
Yes, yes there has been.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:37.040
and my number 1 WTF Moment - Joffrey Dies

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:41.349
If it wasn’t clear, he choked to death.

00:03:41.349 --> 00:03:47.280
The poison was called The Strangler, because
choking and when it’s made it looks purple.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:49.810
That’s why this is called the purple wedding.

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:54.360
Because Joffrey is killed with “purple”
poison.

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:59.800
The show is probably going to reveal the real
truth eventually, so I won’t go all CSI

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:03.450
and point out all the details yet.

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:10.989
The show wants us to think Tyrion did it,
but we saw he was confused when he picked

00:04:10.989 --> 00:04:14.290
up the goblet at the end.

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:16.700
So he has no idea what happened.

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:20.690
Did you catch that shot of Lady Olenna when
he grabbed the goblet for Joffrey a few moments

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:21.690
earlier.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:23.560
She was not staring daggers anymore.

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:25.220
The death scene itself was amazing, prolonged
and intense.

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:29.560
I didn’t count, but they cut back to his
face several times and the camera just lingered.

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:34.070
They really want us to understand that he
suffered horribly, which is good.

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:42.570
But the image is so disturbing that you have
a hard time enjoying the moment.

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:47.590
So now it’s your turn, let me know what
your biggest WTF moments were and what your

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:49.389
reaction to Joffrey dying was.

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:54.220
There was this really interesting thing George
RR Martin said, he mourns his villains just

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:56.770
as much as he mourns killing heros.

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:58.440
Just like you would mourn a real person.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:03.210
He explained that as bad as they are, villains
serve a purpose in the story and once they’re

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:05.360
gone, they’re hard to replace.

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:10.720
So the next big question we need to ask is,
who will replace Joffrey’s role in the story.

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:12.150
As the most hated character.

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:17.539
I nominate Ramsay Snow, but write your own
suggestions in the comments for new WORST

00:05:17.539 --> 00:05:18.539
character.

00:05:18.539 --> 00:05:23.280
Overall the episode as a solid A, Game of
Thrones has the best sets and the best costumes.

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:28.470
And the music, the way they kept using Rains
of Castamere was so haunting.

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:33.540
Even if you didn’t know Joffrey would die,
the music just made you feel creepy and wierd.

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:37.410
Like the universe didn’t want this wedding
to be a success.

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:40.130
They did this really awesome thing with the
set design.

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:44.510
In every single baquet shot, there’s the
image of a lion in the background.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:46.310
Wherever the camera turns.

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:51.030
My favorite one was the shot where it looked
like the Lion was eating Loras’ head.

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:54.100
As for character development, I love Ramsay’s
relationship with Roose Bolton.

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:58.180
He may be evil, but Ramsay still treats him
like a son and gives him a chance to earn

00:05:58.180 --> 00:05:59.180
the Bolton name.

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:04.140
I have to say that when Ramsay and Locke talked
about cutting Jaime’s hand off, it was almost

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:07.270
a more evil moment than the dwarf skull fuck*ng
the wolf’s head.

00:06:07.270 --> 00:06:11.009
Lady Olenna and Tywin’s scene just oozed
with foreshadowing, just two of the best actors

00:06:11.009 --> 00:06:12.810
on the show.

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:18.910
Aren’t you wondering whether or not Tywin’s
going to have any fun before he dies?

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:25.480
Who knew that Cersei would be jealous of Brienne
despite kind of dumping Jaime last week and

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:32.120
aside from them I just love the direction
Bran’s character is going.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:36.260
He’s slowly trying to just completely leave
his body so he can be whole again.

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:39.920
I can’t wait to see what his scenes with
the three eye raven are like.

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:41.460
Let me know what your final thoughts are on
the episode.

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:44.880
One of the worst villains on the show is gone,
but evil abhors a vacuum, so who is going

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.199
to replace him?

00:06:46.199 --> 00:06:49.729
If not on the Iron Throne then somewhere else
in the story.

00:06:49.729 --> 00:06:50.889
The Thenn’s seem pretty evil.

00:06:50.889 --> 00:06:52.460
The King is Dead, Long Live The King.

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:58.780
So Q&amp;A will post tomorrow, I’ll be picking
a random subscriber in the comments to be

00:06:58.780 --> 00:06:59.930
the week 2 giveaway winner.

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:02.260
I’ll announce who in that Monday video.

00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:11.320
And like I said, next week unless something
way more interesting comes up I’ll do a

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:12.880
bloodraven greenseer bonus video.

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:19.790
Right now click here for that Q&amp;A and click
here for my bonus purple wedding video.

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:22.810
Just explaining it a little more in depth.

00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:25.120
Thanks for watching, go hug someone you love.

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:25.659
High Fives!

